{
  "lead": "Dominated by routine administrative filings rather than material news: AuKing lodged a compliance supplement on its Tundulu diamond hole logging, while NexGen filed its monthly CDI reconciliation, neither containing new mineralisation or financial results.",
  "subtitle": "A quiet window of compliance housekeeping, with no assay or financial results.",
  "subject": "AKN files Tundulu mineral abundance supplement, no assays yet",
  "watch_items": [
    "AKN: Assay results from hole 26NH023 at Tundulu expected within 5 to 6 weeks, to confirm whether logged carbonatite intervals carry mineralisation."
  ],
  "day_in_brief": "Drilling and compliance: AuKing lodged a supplement to its 1 September 2026 release on hole 26NH023 at Tundulu, adding visual mineral abundance estimates required under ASX Compliance Update 04.23. Logged intervals at approximately 368 to 370.5m and 381m show apatite calcite carbonatite, with calcite up to ~75%, apatite up to ~10% and pyrite up to ~5%. No mineralisation has yet been reported, with assay results expected within 5 to 6 weeks. Corporate and securities: NexGen's Appendix 4A for August 2026 showed CDIs on issue over quoted securities fell by 9,897,131 to 127,774,907, reflecting net transfers between CDIs and shares quoted on the TSX and NYSE. Common shares without CDIs rose by 10,328,797 to 543,162,860, options on issue declined by 519,999 to 46,908,164, and convertible debentures were unchanged at 39,571,350. Overall, the window carried no drilling results, resource updates or funding news, with both filings administrative in nature.",
